        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Concordia Station",
            "zh": "康宏站"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Antarctica",
            "zh": "南极洲"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " is one of the coldest places on Earth. Snow covers the ground. Sometimes, the sun can’t be seen for months."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The station is home to a group of "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "European",
            "zh": "欧洲的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "scientists",
            "ref": "v-scientist"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Two of them are Cyprien Verseux from France, and Carmen Possnig from "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Austria",
            "zh": "奥地利"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". One day, they took their food outside. They wanted to show what -80℃ to -70℃ felt like, and the cold "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "froze",
            "ref": "v-freeze"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " their "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "spaghetti",
            "zh": "意大利细面条"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "cheese",
            "ref": "v-cheese"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", fried eggs and honey hard all at once."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Do you know how the scientists "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "store",
            "ref": "v-store"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " their food? They "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "bury",
            "ref": "v-bury"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " much of their food in the snow. Possnig said they "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "missed",
            "zh": "怀念"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " having "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "fresh",
            "ref": "v-fresh"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " fruits and vegetables the most. They hadn’t had any for months."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The group once had three and a half months of night. “The night sky was beautiful. We have never seen so many stars before,” said Possnig. “For me, just living here is a "
          },
          {
